    <main class="container">
        <div class="grid-full-page">
            <div>
                <div class="full-width-card">
                    <h2>Wellbeing Issues</h2>
                    <p>Adolescents in New Zealand face multifaceted psychological and physical challenges stemming from unmoderated digital media and late-night device exposure.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="full-width-card">
                    <h3>Sleep Disruption & Anxiety</h3>
                    <p>Blue light and late notifications interfere with natural circadian rhythms, while constant social comparison (FOMO) elevates stress levels among teens.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="full-width-card">
                    <h2>Effect on NZ Teenagers</h2>
                    <p>The <strong>Youth19 Survey</strong> indicates that approximately 22% of NZ teens exhibit problematic use patterns, with nearly half reporting daily disruptions to homework, chores, and rest.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="full-width-card">
                    <h2>Impact on Communities</h2>
                    <p>When peer groups and family interactions are displaced by screen isolation, community engagement and interpersonal empathy decline across society.</p>
                    <div class="citation-box">
                        <strong>Sources Cited:</strong> Youth19 Survey Research Reports; PHCC Aotearoa.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <aside class="visual-sidebar">
                <img src="/static/images/youth_stats.png" alt="New Zealand Youth Wellbeing Statistics">
                <p><strong>Figure 2:</strong> Youth19 Survey wellbeing statistics in Aotearoa.</p>
            </aside>
        </div>
    </main>

